      "mergedPostDetails": "I originally submitted this as feedback directly from TestFlight, but recently I realized I should submit it here too.\n\nIn the original screen that shows up when you first launch the app, when you go to the social tab, at first it sorts our friends list alphabetically. When you reload it, friends from your favorites lists show up at the top. Which is really nice.\n\nBut when you scroll down far enough that new friends need to be loaded in, it refreshes the entire page and sorts the entire list alphabetically again. So if I keep scrolling to the bottom, I would miss a good amount of my online friends because they showed up further up than where I was already looking on my friends list when the page is refreshed.\n\nI need to scroll all the way to the bottom, and then scroll *back up* to the top to review all the names I missed.\n\nAnd then when I scroll to the top again and refresh the page, it sorts it by favorites again, so I would need to repeat the entire process again to review friends whose names appear earlier alphabetically who are *not* on my favorites list if I already refreshed the page.\n\nIt would be nice if it would retain the same order when new friends are loaded in, so I wouldn't need to do this process every time I check my friends list.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Friends List Gets Reordered After Scrolling Down",
